From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:38:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] Local: VICTORY_KEEP_GONE: a texture picked by index
 keeps its last view while its memory is away (off by default)

The pass over textures picked by index made a slot's host view null when
the title had unmapped the texture's memory ("streamed out"), and
uploaded it again when the memory came back: in b43run2 that was 98,064
slots, seen as door and window frames going texture, black, texture
while the game streams from a hard disk.

VICTORY_KEEP_GONE=1 skips that: the slot keeps showing its last host
texture while the memory is away; it is still queued again
(texture_slot_later) and uploaded when the memory returns. A number
above 1 keeps the view for that many frames from the pass that first
found it away, then makes it null as before. In both forms the view is
made null at once while the card is over its video-memory budget (asked
once a frame), since a kept view keeps its host copy from being let go.
A log line every 4,096 looks counts the looks that kept a view, those
that made it null, and the slots away now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
